st a real showman whose life  was as fascinating as it was short  this is a story of one of history's most  colourful forgotten characters a man who  defied every expectation of his class  and era in order to be exactly who he  wanted to be no matter the cost  henry was born on the 16th of june 1875  to the fourth marquess of anglesey and  his second wife blanche mary boyd  there were whispers that henry's  biological father was actually renowned  french actor  benoir constant coccola and considering  the love of the stage that would later  dominate henry's life  that seems plausible tragically when  henry was two years old his mother  passed away and he was sent to paris to  be raised in the cocker law household  further fueling those rumors about the  identity of his father  henry was to live in paris until the age  of eight when he returned to his  ancestral home on the island of anglesey  even at such a young age he was said to  be very different to his peers  and not just due to a love of smelly  cheese he'd picked up in france  a somewhat lonely childhood followed  spent mainly in the company of a nanny  and the many dogs which belong to the  estate before henry's stereotypical  aristocratic upbringing was completed  with surprise surprise and education at  eaton  in 1898 aged 23 henry ticked the next  box on the blue blood checklist by  marrying his cousin lillian chetwin  in october of the same year his father  passed away making henry the fifth  marquis of anglesey and one of the  wealthiest men in britain  [Music]  the family home and estates covered  around 30 000 acres in various parts of  the uk and we're valued at 535 000  pounds  somewhere north of 70 million pounds in  today's money  oh and there's also the small matter of  his annual income of approximately 120  000 pounds  16 million pounds today  just think about that for a moment  16 million pounds a year  that's more than 1.3 million pounds a  month  most people would struggle to get  through that kind of money even if they  weren't really trying but henry was  certainly not most people  in fact spending money may well have  been his true calling  because despite this almost unfathomable  wealth  in fewer than six years  he would be bankrupt  [Music]  at this point in the video i thought  about going through a hypothetical list  of all the things you could buy for that  squandered cash  but henry's real list of excessive  spending  doesn't really need any spicing up  for starters he bought the content of an  entire jewelry shop in paris for his new  wife whilst they run their honeymoon  the story goes that henry asked his  bride to pose wearing the jewels  and nothing else  kind of like every teenage boy's  favorite scene in titanic only without  the token artwork henry marvelled at the  glittering diamonds emeralds and  sapphires covering his wife's body  but before you get the wrong idea there  certainly weren't any pearl necklaces on  show  the marriage was apparently never  consummated and lilian requested its  annulment in 1900  freed from the constraints of matrimony  henry threw himself headlong into his  real passions theater and unadulterated  self-indulgence  the family chapel on the estate was  refurbished to become a 150-seat theater  called the gaiety and henry formed a  theater company poaching actors from  another touring group with promises of  substantially more pay  naturally henry cast himself as the lead  in pretty much every production  but hugging the spotlight wasn't quite  enough to satisfy his narcissistic  tendencies  he wanted to shine in every possible way  costumes for his lavish productions  caused eye-watering sums  apparently he'd never heard of costume  jewelry and he frequently commissioned  bespoke pieces from leading costumias  including a diamond-encrusted outfit for  a production of aladdin that cost 10 000  pounds more than 1.3 million pounds  today sadly that very same aladdin  costume was left unattended in a  changing room and  shock horror never seen again not one to  dwell on the negatives in life  henry simply had another one made  the stolen aladdin outfit wasn't the  only time henry was relieved of some of  his bling in 1901 his valet was charged  with theft pocketing over two million  pounds worth of henry's jewels  it's fair to say that henry was spending  money faster than mike tyson on a  cocaine bender  but he was so incredibly rich that to  bring about full-on bankruptcy  he was going to have to get creative  and oh my the lens henry would go to to  achieve self-imposed financial ruin  were insane  for starters he owned a fleet of  expensive motor cars one of which was  modified to pump perfume out of its  exhaust  yet another of his cars was modeled on a  luxury train carriage  complete with revolving chairs solid  silver fittings and cherubs carved into  the wood paneled ceiling  henry was delighted by all things  glittering and ostentatious so when he  decided he wanted a green ping-pong  jacket it naturally had to be made out  of emeralds  don't worry i had no idea a ping pong  jacket was a thing either considering  henry's flamboyant persona failed  marriage fabulous tastes and risque  outfits there was widespread speculation  about his sexuality not that henry  really gave a bedazzled hoot the more  people talked the more outrageous he  became during the intervals of his shows  he'd perform what was known as the  butterfly dance a habit that earned him  the title the dancing marquess the dance  was based on one made famous by american  actress louis fuller during which a  billowing silky gown would be used to  create movements reminiscent of a  butterfly spreading its wings and flying  of course there's no reason why a  straight man couldn't perform that dance  but this was the early 20th century and  things simply weren't done that way  it wasn't just whilst treading the  boards that henry wanted to stand out  off stage his dress sense was outrageous  often accessorized with a glamorously  groomed poodle  for some it seemed obvious henry was gay  but in truth there's no real evidence to  say he had any lovers men or women  some historians believe he was simply a  pure narcissist capable of only loving  himself  regardless he was certainly unafraid to  be himself and refused to be hemmed in  by the strict norms of victorian or  edwardian society  something that must have taken  incredible courage  don't forget homosexuality was very much  illegal in britain at the time  [Music]  after honing his on-stage craft by  entertaining the anglesey locals henry  took his fear to company on a three-year  tour across the uk and europe there  wasn't too much focus on financial  returns and it was more about putting on  the best shows ever  to his credit henry took things pretty  seriously and he was said to be an  accomplished actor the touring company  was made up of around 50 individuals  including actors an orchestra and  support workers  they travelled with their own specially  painted scenery and furniture as well as  elaborate costumes all of which was  transported in five large trucks  henry also employed a personal staff of  four and considering he made more  costume changes than beyonce  they probably worked harder than anyone  else in the company it's not hard to  imagine that the cost of running this  theater company coupled with henry's  lifestyle in general would eventually  lead to dire monetary consequences  initially henry started mortgaging his  properties to make ends meet but things  snowballed pretty quickly with his  unabated spending  by 1904 he'd accumulated debts of around  560 000 pounds over 72 million pounds  today and bankruptcy proceedings were  started  with trustees in charge of henry's  financial affairs  everything went under the hammer at a  series of auctions that would span 40  days  according to one newspaper it was the  most wonderful collection of clothing  ever sold  and judging by most of the surviving  pictures of henry it's hard to disagree  with that one  all told it took a good 40 days for the  auctioneers to work their way through  henry's many possessions  one whole day was needed just to sell  his huge collection of dogs  and it took more than several to work  through his otherworldly collection of  dressing gowns furs and over 900 silk  lined suits  for the most part the auction was a  roaring success henry's colossal  jewellery collection fetched 80 000  pounds alone  and by the time the hammer fell on the  final lot he was actually left in profit  which was provided for him in the form  of an annual pension of two thousand  pounds a year or about two hundred and  sixty thousand pounds in today's money  [Music]  now to the vast majority of us that  would still count as a huge fortune  more than enough to fund an extremely  affluent lifestyle  it doesn't buy you all that many emerald  ping-pong jackets though does it  according to one newspaper henry was so  unhappy with his new more modest  circumstances that he concocted a plan  to beat the house at the famous monte  carlo casino  a plan that you won't be surprised to  hear failed miserably  henry's final curtain call came in the  form of tb and after a drawn-out illness  he passed away in the monte carlo hotel  with his estranged wife by his side  without an heir or siblings the title of  marquess and what was left of the family  estate were passed on to henry's cousin  charles padgett  not that his family were in any way sad  to see henry go  almost without exception they were  deeply ashamed of henry  so much so that after his death they did  everything they could to erase him from  their history  destroying almost all of his personal  effects including his diaries letters  and any other traces of him  henry's theatre became a chapel again  and all the other changes he'd made to  the family's land and properties were  undone one by one  the national trust became the guardians  of the family home in the 1970s  and for a long time there were only a  few photocopied pictures of henry placed  near a toilet  but in 2017 an iconic picture of henry  was used on the cover of a book which  explored the national trust lgbt history  and the limelight returns to this  flamboyant character  thanks to his family's attempts to  strike henry from the history books  we're left with a bit of an enigma of a  man but henry is finally starting to get  some of the attention he craved in life  if you ask me the world is a better  place with crazy extravagant people in  it and i like to think that if henry was  alive today he'd be posting a  ridiculously cheesy picture of himself  on a beach at sunset complete with the  words if you're going to dance then make  sure everybody is watching and give them  a show they'll never forget and unlike  most people who post that crap henry  would actually have the lifestyle to  back it up  [Music]  thanks for watching
 

